class RPPController(Node):
    """
    Straight-segment precision controller: constant-speed field-test build.

    Every non-zero horizontal velocity-vector command uses exactly 0.40 m/s.

    Constant-speed contract:
      - C->P1 travel: 0.40 m/s.
      - Generated 50 mm pass-through travel: 0.40 m/s.
      - Segment alignment: 0.40 m/s.
      - Cross-track recovery: 0.40 m/s.
      - Terminal alignment and final approach: 0.40 m/s.
      - PX4 native pivot: continuously command the fixed segment velocity vector.
      - No acceleration ramp, deceleration, heading speed reduction,
        terminal speed reduction, creep speed, or translation pulse.
      - Literal zero remains for emergency stop, mission disable, stale
        localization, exact marking stop, and safety-hold conditions.

    Geometry retained:
      - Fixed C->P1 capture line.
      - Generated 50 mm pass-through guidance.
      - Global cross-track priority at 30 mm.
      - Exact marking stop latch at measured radial distance <=30 mm.
      - Existing capture-missed safe hold.
      - PX4 native pivot begins when true segment error reaches 45 deg.
      - PX4 changes from pivot to straight travel at 12 deg or less.
      - There is no 6 degree release gate and no zero-speed alignment hold.
      - Moving straight-line correction is limited to +/-12 deg.
      - C->P1 follows active generated 50 mm interpolation targets while
        retaining one fixed bearing from captured current position to P1.
      - Dedicated monitor topics publish signed cross-track error, exact-goal
        radial distance, along-track remaining and closest distance in mm.

    This build is intended only for a controlled speed test.
    """

